et code within each school, the administrative department name, the average clearing cost collector, the variance of the clearing cost collector, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the clearing cost collector, and the most recent activity date for the administrative department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3215\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012, show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code, for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3590\", \"desc\": \"Show, for each subject, the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null; and for subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a cluster type of 'S', show the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED, the offer department name, the total units from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title. Indicate the source of each row as either 'Subq1' or 'Subq2'. List all results together, showing the columns: subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, dense rank by school, offer department name, total units, row number window, and source, in that order, ordered by subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3828\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject code description, and the row number of each course within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by course description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3248\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1471\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject title, department name, school name, and the rank within each school name group ordered by subject code, but only include those subjects whose total units exceed the average total units for their respective school. Additionally, for the Mathematics department, also show the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects that are offered this year, are letter graded, and are in the Mathematics department), as well as the number of subjects that are Communication Intensive (i.e., have a non-null COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE), with these statistics included for each subject in the result. Present the columns in the following order: subject code, subject title, department name, school name, rank within school, average total units, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and number of Communication Intensive subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}]}}"
